== waiting
brief: What every customer says while they wait and the player looks elsewhere. They climb through the moods, calmest first.
(neutral) Hello...
(neutral) Hi?
(neutral) Hello there?
(neutral) Anyone here?
(neutral) Hi, um... I have a computer?
(neutral) Is the shop open?
(neutral) The sign said open...
(neutral) Knock knock?

(thinking) Are you there?
(thinking) Is anybody back there?
(thinking) Hmm... hello?
(thinking) Maybe they're in the back.
(thinking) Should I ring the bell again?
(thinking) Did I come on the wrong day?
(thinking) This is the computer shop, right?
(thinking) I can hear someone in there...

(irritated01) Hello?
(irritated01) Excuse me...
(irritated01) Hello-o?
(irritated01) Excuse me, sir?
(irritated01) Um. Hello?
(irritated01) I'm right here.
(irritated01) Could I get some help, please?
(irritated01) Yoo-hoo?

(irritated02) Are you busy?
(irritated02) I'm still waiting here.
(irritated02) Can someone help me?
(irritated02) I've been standing here a while.
(irritated02) Is this a bad time?
(irritated02) My parking runs out soon.
(irritated02) Hello? HELLO?
(irritated02) I can wait. I guess.

(irritated03) I can go somewhere else.
(irritated03) I don't have all day.
(irritated03) Unbelievable.
(irritated03) Some service this is.
(irritated03) I'll take it to the place across town.
(irritated03) Is this how you treat customers?
(irritated03) Do you even work here?
(irritated03) Fine. FINE. I'll just stand here.
